(docs/BUGS_FOUND.md #109. Nested collections are pointer-in (see
 REPORT-109.md), so a list holding the SAME nested list through two slots
 would have the walk try to free that nested block twice in one `Free` call
 - the second attempt would be a read of already-unmapped memory. The
 `_free_visit_or_skip` dedup table (list.asm), reset fresh by codegen
 before each top-level `Free`, records a pointer the first time this call
 tree frees it and skips it on any later slot that names the same pointer.
 This test only proves the crash does not happen; it does not distinguish
 that from the OTHER, deliberately out-of-scope aliasing hazard (a
 separate named variable still pointing at a freed nested block) - see the
 report.)

a list called inner is [1, 2].
a list called outer is [inner, inner, 99].
print outer's length.
Free outer.
print "no crash".
print outer's length.
